{"title":"Topicwise Test-19 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics-1","fileName":"071_Topicwise Test-19 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics-1.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements is/are not correct about a multiplexer (MUX) circuit?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> A MUX is a sequential circuit.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n A 2<sup>n</sup> input lines MUX has n-output lines.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> A MUX circuit can be designed using AND and NOT gates.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> A MUX circuit can be used as a universal logic gate.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b)<br />\n &bull; A MUX is a combinational circuit since it has no feedback element present.<br />\n &bull; A MUX has only 1 output line.<br />\n &bull; An AND and a NOT gate can form a complete set and can be used as a universal gate.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the MUX circuit shown below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f29f8fd80e9b2d573723774288cba006d2a265e7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The Boolean function realized by the above circuit is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ecd580ff71a46e1ea3d88dc466baeb8ee40a1d27.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/f82df7c0cc6d602be9fc97bb88fde5a4eda40aa4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a027ad242f6b88d615d17e09ec4aab350bc02a74.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5e50e04e8a855db4a7e6588a7beedfaba25a6b34.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/022d60fa3344273ea8719326ef69ac7d0e217b99.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The average propagation delay of each MUX is 35 ns. The frequency of the output signal <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> is ______ MHz.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8278d225bef405be7befcc51fffbfbf643c94f9d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.7","high":"4.85"},"solution":"<p>\n 4.76 (4.70 - 4.85)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/81ddfad24261a846fbc0c69da9f995acc931cf74.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A 32 : 1 MUX has to be designed using a 16 : 1 MUX. It was found that for this task we require ‘<em>X</em>’ number of 16 : 1 MUX and “<em>Y</em>” number of two input OR gates, then the value of <em>X</em> + <em>Y</em> = _____ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>\n 3</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3aff795ec692430b11cc4c63523e0f01590f8430.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A logical function is given as</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a906173dca29b14a6a225232c1f2fc4d33845187.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The number of essential prime implicants in the given function will be _______ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>\n 2</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4fa1f47d5cfeb5787610efe5d39771eb69fbb8ca.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A three variable Boolean function is defined as <em>f</em>(<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>) = Σ<em>m</em>(1, 2, 5, 6). If <img src=\"/media/4135b5da2b6c22def3425b7e71603462759e6571.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> denotes the compliment of the function <em>f</em> (<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>), then the simplified expression of <img src=\"/media/e962b573e3cee79bda2d34f276d120d09b79a99e.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> can be given as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/9f54e4866b8d59b28d46455f16cfb013cf26479a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1df45c5dafbf818f92be8a60d32ef649c068603b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/fdd02ff4071887d9a07ad23f8938a798af2d1b7e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c7d62c7aeda176780c8b7f07528881b3fd502f57.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/23e4aaad77f5aab1173f1d307dbaea4e95d3b936.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A 1-bit full adder takes 10 ns to generate output carry bit and 20 ns to generate the output sum bit. If four such full adders are cascaded to form a 4-bit parallel adder, then the maximum number of 4-bit additions per second that can be performed by the parallel adder is _____ × 10<sup>6</sup>.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"20","high":"20"},"solution":"<p>\n 20</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/769a829a386ae648e52f78c3583e39e929dc3417.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The map for a Boolean function <em>F</em> is shown in figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5daeeabfbbf4e944c5467b979ee96d689e4a3ebb.png\" loadi